<article class="prose-izumi"><p class="eyebrow">Companion</p><h1>Set up Samsung Tizen</h1><p class="lede">Install izumi Companion, pair it with izumi, and make future updates happen from the TV.</p>
<h2>What you need</h2><ul><li>A Samsung TV running Tizen 2.3 or newer.</li><li>A Windows, macOS, or Linux computer — or an Android/iPhone installer — on the same local network.</li><li>A Samsung account for first-time installation.</li><li>izumi installed on your phone or computer.</li></ul>
<aside class="callout"><strong>On-TV updates</strong><br />Automatic TV updates require Tizen 3.0 or newer with Web service support. Older TVs can still run Companion; update them with the installer.</aside>
<h2>Install and pair</h2><ol><li>Download the latest <a href="https://github.com/nickEatsBread/izumiCompanion/releases/latest">izumi Companion Installer</a>.</li><li>On the TV, open Apps or Apps Settings and enter <code>12345</code> to enable Developer Mode.</li><li>Set Host PC IP to the computer’s local address, restart the TV, and find its TV IP under Network Status → IP Settings.</li><li>Enter the TV IP in the installer, choose <strong>Connect TV</strong>, then <strong>Install on TV</strong>.</li><li>When setup completes, open Companion and pair it with izumi using the QR code or short pairing code.</li></ol>
<h2>Enable updates on the TV</h2><p>After the installer confirms setup, return to Developer Mode and change Host PC IP to <code>127.0.0.1</code>. Restart the TV, then open Companion. Keep the installer’s Samsung signing identity backed up: the same identity is needed to replace the app without losing pairing and progress.</p>
